    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "Perfect! The fix is complete and working. Here's what I found:\n\n**Root cause:** The `parseEuros` function was doing `Number * 100` which caused floating-point precision loss. For example, `39.95 * 100 = 3995.0000000000005` instead of `3995`.\n\n**The fix:** Changed line 13 in `src/money.js` from:\n```javascript\nreturn Number(Number(s.replace(/,/g, '')).toFixed(2)) * 100;\n```\nto:\n```javascript\nreturn Math.round(Number(s.replace(/,/g, '')) * 100);\n```\n\n`Math.round()` rounds the result to the nearest integer, giving us exactly `3995` instead of `3995.0000000000005`. All tests pass, and edge cases like \u20ac0.01, \u20ac99.99, and \u20ac39.95 work correctly now.",
